Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity => { /* app losing focus */ })
        .OnStop(activity => { /* app fully backgrounded */ }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app => { /* app backgrounded */ }));
#endif
});
```

**Platform mapping:** Android `OnPause` ≈ iOS `WillResignActive` (lost focus), and Android `OnStop` ≈ iOS `DidEnterBackground` (fully hidden).

**Cross-platform alternative:** If you don't need the native callback parameters, override `OnStopped` on your `Window` subclass — it maps to `OnStop` on Android and `DidEnterBackground` on iOS automatically:

```csharp
protected override void OnStopped()
{
    base.OnStopped();
    // runs on both platforms when app is no longer visible
}
```

**Tips:**
- Keep handlers fast (<2s) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS.
- On Android, the back button can skip `Stopped` entirely — also save in `OnDestroying`.
